#: card/card/report/project_invoice_profitability/project_invoice_profitability.py:66
msgid "Read only. Revenue is the net amount of submitted Sales Invoice lines, by posting date, in the company currency. Expenses are the net amount of the submitted Purchase Invoice lines that are booked to an Expense account and are neither a stock item nor a fixed asset. The other Purchase Invoice lines (stock items, fixed-asset items, lines booked to an account that is not an Expense account) are in the column \"Purchases not in expenses\": it is information only and is not in the margin. Stock that was bought and consumed, for example diesel or spare parts bought as stock items, is therefore not in the project expenses of this report, so the margin can be higher than the real one. Opening invoices are not read. A line without a project takes the project of its invoice; lines with no project at all are on the row \"No project\". Journal entries and the general ledger are not read, and nothing is estimated. The margin is revenue minus purchase-invoice expenses, not the full net profit: payroll, depreciation, overhead and journal-entry costs are not included."
msgstr ""

